## 🎁 What's New in Release 1.00: Product Voids & Retail Arbitrage

Release 1.00 introduces specialized natural language scrapers and synthesis engines tracking consumer expressions of:
> *"Ojalá vendieran esto en México..."* | *"Por qué no hay en México..."* | *"Mandar a traer del gabacho..."* | *"Me lo retuvo la aduana..."*

### Tracked Product Voids & Missing Goods
* **Countertop Compact Dishwashers (Hava, Farberware):** High demand in small CDMX/Roma apartments; blocked by Mexican retail stocking only 24" full-size units and NOM energy certification customs deposits.
* **Trader Joe's Specialty Foods & Seasonings:** Everything Bagel, Chili Onion Crunch commanding 400% markups on Instagram grey-market resellers.
* **High-Potency Melatonin (5-10mg) & Kirkland Bulk Antihistamines:** 365-count bottles absent in Mexican farmacias due to COFEPRIS OTC classification restrictions.
* **Matter / Zigbee No-Neutral Smart Relays:** Specialized smart-home hardware adapted to Mexican residential conduit lacking neutral wire.
* **Compact Tropical Dehumidifiers:** Desiccant/refrigerant units with continuous drainage for extreme Yucatán limestone moisture and mold prevention.
* **Japanese & Korean Ultralight Sunscreens (Biore UV, Skin Aqua):** Photostable next-gen UV filters absent in domestic drugstore inventories.
* **Automated Self-Cleaning Cat Litter Boxes (Litter-Robot, Petkit):** 200%+ scalper markups and lack of domestic technical repair networks.
* **Port of Progreso Maritime Consolidation:** Direct Gulf shipping bypass for Yucatán expats and builders avoiding CDMX customs bottlenecks.

